        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: دقت",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دقت — diqqat — \"a difficulty; a hassle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اگر کوئی دقت ہے تو مجھے بتائیے۔ agar koī diqqat hai to mujhe batāiye. If there is any difficulty, tell me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دقت (diqqat) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic diqqa, \"fineness, exactness\"; Urdu uses it for a difficulty or a hassle, a sense our sources do not trace."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
